Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-cadence: add Axera AX630C compatible

The AX630C (AX620E family) integrates a stock Cadence SD4HC: HRS at the
window base, the SDHCI-compatible SRS block at +0x200, the HRS04 PHY access
port and the HRS06 mode/tune field all exactly as this driver expects. Its
PHY delay values come from the standard cdns,phy-* properties.

The one thing it needs told is SDHCI_QUIRK2_PRESET_VALUE_BROKEN. The
controller's preset registers are populated rather than blank, but with
values that do not describe this board's PHY; the vendor's own fork of this
driver selects the same quirk.

No init hook. The DLL reset pulse the vendor driver issues before writing PHY
parameters is already performed by the boot firmware, which reads the kernel
off this controller before Linux starts.

Issue #76 of the open-nanokvm-pro mainline port. Intended for upstream once
the axera vendor prefix settles on LKML (see the AX650 series, v2 2026-09-01).

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -500,6 +500,20 @@
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * Axera AX630C. Stock SD4HC: the HRS/SRS layout, the HRS04 PHY port and the
+ * HRS06 mode/tune field are all as this driver already expects. The only
+ * integration the SoC needs is the preset quirk -- the vendor's own driver
+ * selects it too -- because the controller's preset registers are populated
+ * with values that do not describe this board's PHY.
+ */
+static const struct sdhci_cdns_drv_data sdhci_cdns_ax630c_drv_data = {
+	.pltfm_data = {
+		.ops = &sdhci_cdns_ops,
+		.quirks2 = SDHCI_QUIRK2_PRESET_VALUE_BROKEN,
+	},
+};
+
 static const struct sdhci_cdns_drv_data sdhci_cdns_drv_data = {
 	.pltfm_data = {
 		.ops = &sdhci_cdns_ops,
@@ -653,6 +667,10 @@
 		.compatible = "mobileye,eyeq-sd4hc",
 		.data = &sdhci_eyeq_drv_data,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "axera,ax630c-sd4hc",
+		.data = &sdhci_cdns_ax630c_drv_data,
+	},
 	{ .compatible = "cdns,sd4hc" },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
